CM_ "PROVISIONAL, DOCUMENTATION-ONLY vendor DBC for the ENNOID BMS in its VESC status protocol (BMS Tool: Load status protocol = VESC), the M25 unit's setting (firmware 6.6, CAN ID 10, VESC ID style, 500 kbit/s; 2026-10-12). Layouts from the newest public source, the ENNOID branch of EnnoidMe/ENNOID-BMS-Firmware (V5.2, modCANSendStatusVESC); TODO(capture): confirm against the 6.6 unit. Everything is sent once per second as one burst; all multi-byte fields are big-endian. Float signals are VESC float32_auto, bit-identical to IEEE-754 single. The firmware decoder is firmware/lib/ennoid/src/ennoid_vesc.c and does NOT use this file. Not wired into dbc/generate.py. Not listed: AH_WH (0x280A) and BAL (0x2A0A).";
CM_ BO_ 2147493386 "1 Hz. Pack voltage = sum of cells on M25. ChargerVoltage is the BMS's charger-input measurement.";
CM_ BO_ 2147493642 "1 Hz. MEANINGLESS on M25: the BMS has no current sensor. Not subscribed by the TTCS.";
CM_ BO_ 2147494154 "1 Hz, one frame per 3 cells (108S = 36 frames). CellIndex is the first cell in the frame. Not subscribed by the TTCS (the summary carries min/max).";
CM_ BO_ 2147494666 "1 Hz, one frame per 3 sensors; the last frame is shorter (DLC 4/6/8) when the count isn't a multiple of 3. EVERY channel the BMS reports, enabled or not. The TTCS uses the minimum for the charger's cold-charge check only.";
CM_ BO_ 2147494922 "1 Hz. BMS board temperatures and humidity. Not subscribed by the TTCS.";
CM_ BO_ 2147495178 "1 Hz. CAN_PACKET_BMS_SOC_SOH_TEMP_STAT. TempCellMax is the BMS's own maximum over its ENABLED sensors (1 degC resolution): the TTCS over-temperature input. ChargeAllowed (b2) feeds the TTCS charge enforcement and the charger. There is no discharge-allowed flag in this protocol.";
CM_ BO_ 2147486243 "TTCS -> ENNOID safety keep-alive, fixed literal ID 0x0A23 (checked before node-ID filtering). The BMS only acts on it with 'Use Safety CAN Input' on (off on M25). TTCS sends 0x0F every 1 s.";
